    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yo, i'm looking at a 2022 f150 in the shop. transmission is slipping bad. i'm seeing some weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit on the scan tool. what are the most likely culprits for pressure fluctuations like that? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit of your 2022 F-150's transmission are a serious indicator, likely pointing to a few key areas. It's probably not just a simple fluid change; you might be dealing with a failing solenoid or a pressure control valve that's acting up. A clogged or failing pressure relief valve could also be causing those erratic pressure readings, which is a prime suspect when you see inconsistent behavior like slipping. You should check the transmission fluid level and condition first, but be prepared to dig deeper into the electronic control modules and the physical valve body.",
