    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk if its the solenoids. i checked the fluid and looks mostly okay, no burnt smell or anything. but the spikes are really inconsistent. like it'll be fine for a few mins then it just goes haywire. could it be something like debris in the valve body or just some weird electronic glitch in the TCM?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inconsistent spikes, especially when the fluid looks decent, make a debris issue in the valve body a very strong possibility. Debris, even tiny bits, can cause a solenoid to intermittently stick or a spool valve to chatter, leading to those unpredictable pressure fluctuations. It's less likely to be a simple \"glitch,\" but a failing component *within* the TCM or the wiring harness connecting to it is certainly possible. You'd need to check the electrical integrity of those solenoids—continuity, resistance, and voltage signals—to rule out an electronic fault.",
      "source": "target",
